{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), evidence is extremely sparse. The most critical open question for a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether adding an image modality to the RNA baseline actually improves performance. config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the most direct, controlled extension of config_001: it holds the RNA encoder and profile setting constant while introducing the image modality with the simplest standard fusion (concat). This single experiment will (a) establish whether multimodal integration is worthwhile at all, (b) provide a multimodal baseline against which to later compare fusion strategies, image encoders, and profile settings, and (c) reduce the largest source of uncertainty in the design space. If multimodal helps, we exploit that direction; if not, we efficiently rule out an entire branch of the search. No other single experiment reduces uncertainty about this fundamental design choice as cleanly."
}

